id: pm-review-pr7r
title: "Classify Sourcery budget, Sourcery guide and CodeRabbit manual-review notices as informational"
description: "Live acceptance of the packed package against unbraind/pm-vcs#104 imported three non-actionable bot notices as pending findings: Sourcery's review-budget notice, Sourcery's Reviewer's Guide, and CodeRabbit's notice that the repository does not receive automatic reviews. The CodeRabbit notice was also titled with its GitHub admonition marker ([!IMPORTANT]) instead of its text. pm review round then counted them as pending, so a finished round could never complete."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-12T12:35:57.295Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T19:39:08.079Z"
author: claude-orchestrator
acceptance_criteria: All three notice shapes import as informational; a title never starts with a GitHub admonition marker; the regression test fails with the classifier change reverted; npm and bun release gates pass at unchanged coverage.
parent: pm-review-epic
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T12:36:00.426Z",claude-orchestrator,"Revert proof: with src/findings.ts restored to HEAD, test/core.test.ts fails 1 of 11; with the change, 11 of 11 pass. Real notice bodies come from pm-vcs#104 (Sourcery budget and guide, CodeRabbit manual-review notice)."
  "2026-10-13T19:26:21.027Z",codex-agent,"PR 1 finding 3 accepted: cover real provider budget, limit, access and setup notice shapes while preserving substantive findings about limits and scanning. Regression fixtures and behavioral revert proof required."
  "2026-10-13T19:33:27.623Z",codex-agent,"Accepted findings have passing real-tracker regressions. Reverting only the relevant dispatch, classification, import or apply function makes each targeted test fail on the original behavior; fixed functions restored. See docs/pr-1-review-round.md for per-finding evidence and packed dogfood UX."
  "2026-10-13T19:39:06.792Z",codex-agent,"Fix round complete: isolated npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 91/91 tests, 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across 17 sources, zero duplication, production audit, pack, changelog, release attestation and packed npm/native Bun acceptance. All five latest function-only revert proofs fail as expected; fixed functions restored. Packed dogfood re-import created zero duplicates, preserves five explicit fix verdicts, repairs notice and legacy major classifications, and supports repo-only precedent search. Identity gate and added-line privacy checks report zero. See docs/pr-1-review-round.md. Live review actions were not applied."
